      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run anomalous at t=3240 s. Tube pressure has climbed steadily since growth began, from 2.922 to 3.191 Torr, and the rise is speeding up. Argon flow is holding at about 100 sccm, so extra gas isn't the cause.\n\n- **Likely cause:** most likely a furnace or gas-line fault, either a seal leak letting air in or a blocked exhaust. I can't say which, because this furnace has no exhaust O2 sensor. That same missing sensor means the growth atmosphere can't be checked.\n- **Temperature:** normal. It's holding at 750 °C with steady heater power (about 45%).\n- **Sample result:** none yet. No characterization of the sample exists.\n- **Recommended action:** call a human (the run continues regardless). Someone should do a manual leak check, or shut off the argon and watch how fast pressure rises, to tell a leak from a blockage.\n\nEven if the sample later shows growth or no growth, that result shouldn't count as evidence about the recipe unless this pressure problem is cleared up."
     }
    ],
